    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d295">

                <pb facs="0557" n="509" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg509"/>

                <head>No. 295.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee
                        to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-05-24"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 24, 1877</date>.
                        (Received June 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 558.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Today’s Gaceta publishes a bill to be
                    presented to the Cortes by royal order of His Majesty, intended to foster
                    commerce in Spanish bottoms with the Philippine Islands, by conceding, as a
                    bounty, certain reductions from the regular tariff of customs-duties upon
                    foreign merchandise imported into the ports of the Philippines under the Spanish
                    flag.</p>
                <p>This measure has been in abeyance since June, 1871. Its history and character are
                    amply shown in the bill itself, which I transmit herewith, in copy and
                    translation.</p>
                <p>It will probably soon become a law, when I will take care to send you information
                    of its promulgation.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. AUGUSTUS ADEE.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d295-a1.xml" xpointer="d295-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
